% ============================================================================
% past-tense-ed-sound.query.adj — worked recall over the past-tense-ed-sound
% library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "how is this word's -ed
% ending pronounced?" (direct) or "which example word has this -ed sound?"
% (reverse) — it states no fact of its own — it only `import`s the grounded
% table and asks binding queries.
% ============================================================================

import "past-tense-ed-sound.adj"

? past_tense_ed_sound(walked, $Sound)        % expect t_sound (direct)
? past_tense_ed_sound($W, id_sound)          % expect wanted (reverse)
? past_tense_ed_sound(played, $Sound)        % expect abstain -- played is /d/-sounded too, but not one of the three tabled example words
